{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"eb0bee0b65d57af0f24d0ddb691a0af1e9361616d974824b40378f855bc5ce66","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_e187dd568c9b7c2a2832c1fd056b56796ebc85e4723aa11d002f5e5c7455f82d","overall_assessment":"The paper proposes a deep learning framework (MDA) that uses Marginal Fisher Analysis for layer-wise initialization, targeting small and medium-scale datasets. The method is technically coherent, and the experimental design includes a diverse set of datasets and ablation studies. However, the evaluation lacks statistical rigor for most experiments, and the comparison to state-of-the-art methods is limited to a specific set of autoencoder-based models, which may not fully represent the current landscape of deep learning for these tasks.","paper_id":"BysZhEqee","paper_identity_sha256":"06ba4b4b9834ec5861aaf627b1a1ff357373a415a2679f30370a56492707d687","prompt_identity_sha256":"9a698542ed2bd90a508ea171f48566e190d3d3eaaa68a9fe7d4ee59d830002cc","raw_response_sha256":"24600919bff121667aba440a416630d614a8b932ab807129107f78e6573fb2fe","request_identity_sha256":"daefe3120200b183b9b07c1a020f02ad1d226a4bebaddf174b42f302aed8aa39","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"93c9a9c4921144d72358f2c46c49405d2d38cd37a0bbb16540430efcd51eea80","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The proposed Marginal Deep Architectures (MDA) framework is mathematically well-defined. The paper clearly outlines the layer-wise mapping from the input space to the output space, utilizing a random projection for the first layer and Marginal Fisher Analysis (MFA) for subsequent layers. The formulation of the MFA objective function (Equation 4) and the integration of deep learning techniques such as backpropagation, denoising, and dropout are described with sufficient detail to understand the technical process. The method appears to be correctly implemented according to the described architecture, with no apparent conceptual errors in the formulation of the stacked feature learning models.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The experimental design is comprehensive, covering seven different datasets across various domains, including handwritten digits, speech, and image classification. The paper includes ablation studies on the number of hidden layers and the structure of the second layer, which helps in understanding the sensitivity of the model to architectural choices. However, the baselines are limited to autoencoder-based models (AE, SAE, DAE, SDAE) and shallow feature learning methods (PCA, MFA). The comparison to more recent or diverse deep learning architectures, such as convolutional neural networks or recurrent neural networks, is absent, which may limit the generalizability of the claims regarding state-of-the-art performance.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-030","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper provides detailed hyperparameters for the experiments, including minibatch size, learning rate, momentum, dropout rate, and denoising rate. The architecture configurations for each dataset are also specified. However, the paper does not mention the availability of code or provide a link to a repository, which may hinder reproducibility. Additionally, the random seed used for initialization is not specified, which could affect the reproducibility of the results, especially given the use of random projections and dropout.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-029","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper compares MDA against a set of relevant baselines, including autoencoder-based models and shallow feature learning methods. The choice of baselines is appropriate for the context of the paper, which focuses on small and medium-scale applications where deep learning models may struggle. However, the comparison does not include more recent or diverse deep learning architectures, which may limit the strength of the claim that MDA outperforms state-of-the-art methods. The related work section provides a good overview of the field, but the experimental comparison could be expanded to include a broader range of methods.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-031","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037"],"review_text":"The paper reports classification accuracy and error rates for the experiments. However, for most datasets, the results are presented as single values without confidence intervals or standard deviations, which makes it difficult to assess the statistical significance of the improvements. The only exception is the CMU mocap dataset, where standard deviations are reported. The lack of statistical tests or error bars for the other datasets limits the ability to determine whether the observed differences in performance are meaningful or due to random variation.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"c878c6e0ddfcfdee8f031c486260fa72219af3a5b5f9b7334afef62a6d355d36","paper_id":"BysZhEqee","paper_ordinal":81,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"24600919bff121667aba440a416630d614a8b932ab807129107f78e6573fb2fe","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BysZhEqee","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"d89dc2b6707dfb47e3bce0a7d48e9db1d53720ed991499e04749bc33733b18a6","request_identity_sha256":"daefe3120200b183b9b07c1a020f02ad1d226a4bebaddf174b42f302aed8aa39","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1195,"prompt_tokens":19887,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":21082},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"daefe3120200b183b9b07c1a020f02ad1d226a4bebaddf174b42f302aed8aa39","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}